index 663d3991d0907673d180fb7aef544b4165bc368c..19a629acdfa094bc00e42ef28f947b39e4c3c591 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -12,4 +12,14 @@ is malformed (no leading `/`, or a `~` not followed by `0` or `1`) or does not r
 array index out of range or with leading zeros, the `-` end-of-array token, or descent into a scalar.
 Only own members are looked up, so `__proto__` or `toString` never resolve.
 
+## JSON Patch (RFC 6902)
+
+`applyPatch(document, patch)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, applies a JSON Patch (an array of
+`add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and `test` operations) and returns the result as a new
+value; neither the document nor the patch is mutated. It throws an `Error` when the patch is invalid
+(not an array, unknown `op`, missing or non-string `path`/`from`, missing `value`) or when an
+operation fails, including a failed `test`. A patch is atomic: on error nothing is returned.
+Removing the whole document (`remove` with an empty path) is rejected, as is moving a value into its
+own child.
+
 Run the tests with `npm test` (Node 22.18 or later, which runs the TypeScript tests directly).
